{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis","kind":"proposition","title":"The Hecke generators under the Markov trace do not satisfy Blitvić's pair-partition hypothesis","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-non-commutative-probability-dictionary","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-jones-markov-trace"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis"],"cites":["references/blitvic2012","references/wenzl1988"],"tags":["q-clt","blitvic","pair-partition","hecke-quadratic-relation","established"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Observations.hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis","text":"hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> be a field, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in K^\\times</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h = q - q^{-1}</code>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}</code> be a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code>-linear trace on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_1(q)</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}(1) = 1</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}(\\sigma) = z</code>. Put <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde\\sigma := \\sigma - z \\cdot 1</code>. Then</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathrm{tr}\\bigl(\\tilde\\sigma^{2}\\bigr) = h z + 1 - z^{2},\n  \\qquad\n  \\mathrm{tr}\\bigl(\\tilde\\sigma^{3}\\bigr) = (h^{2}+1)\\,z + h - 3 h z^{2} - 3 z + 2 z^{3}.</code></pre>\n<p>Every Markov trace on the Hecke tower restricts to such a trace on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_1(q)</code>. For the Markov parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = q^{3}/(q^{2}+1)</code>, evaluating at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 2</code> gives <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}(\\tilde\\sigma^{3}) = -357/250 \\neq 0</code>.</p>\n<p>So the odd centred moments of the Hecke generators under the Jones–Markov trace do <strong>not</strong> all vanish, and the generators do <strong>not</strong> satisfy the pair-partition hypothesis of Blitvić's non-commutative central limit theorem [<code>blitvic2012</code>], which requires every odd moment to vanish.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"7.3.12","page":"b/prop-hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis","qa":{"counts":{"pass":65,"fail":1,"warn":2,"na":51,"unknown":0,"stale":105},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:HeckeTemperleyLieb.hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.markovTrace_centred_cube_ne_zero","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/HeckeTemperleyLieb/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
